<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The monogram badge AS THE WIDGET PICKER SEES IT, and only there.

    ⚠ A PREVIEW IS A STATIC RESOURCE. Nothing runs for it: no provider, no row factory, no read —
    so it cannot carry the real badge, which is a Bitmap drawn at runtime from the palette in force
    (WidgetMonogram). Hence a flat disc and NO LETTER: an initial here would be an invented
    correspondent, and the picture's job is to show the row's geometry, not to name anybody.

    The colour is @color/widget_unread_count for the same reason the account dot next door uses it:
    it is the accent, the one flat colour the two widgets already draw with, and this is a shape
    rather than a vector because it is one flat fill.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <solid android:color="@color/widget_unread_count" />
</shape>
